{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And it shall be.</b> The Valley of Achor is around Jerusalem, and it is written \"the Valley of Achor for a door of hope\" (Hosea 2:17), and many said it is in the sense of \"the troubler of Israel\" (1 Kings 18:17), but there is no need:" "<b>who sought Me.</b> For He will remember that they sought Him alone:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 65, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:01.855479044Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}